{"text": "CHARGE NUMBER: 2501\nPROJECT TITLE: Nuclear and Radiochemistry of Smoke\nPROJECT LEADER: Roger A. Comes\nPERIOD COVERED: May 1-31, 1982\n\nDATE OF REPORT:\n\ndune 3, 1982\n\nSmoke Studies????***\n\n1. Cigarettes prepared: from the 2R1 filler onto which '*C(U)-3-\nduvatrienediol was sprayed were sectioned and smoked for total distribution\nof radioactivity. Only a limited number (10) of these cigarettes were\navailable. Previously determined theoretical activity was 2.4uCi/g for the\nfiller, Section data yielded a total cigarette activity (singie determination)\nof 2.62uCi (2.22uCi/g). Two of these cigarettes were smoked on the total\nrecovery smoking machine to give the distribution data shown:\n\nin Fraction\n\nRun 1 Run 2 Average\nSS gas 24.1 22.0 23.1\nMS gas 2.9 2.8 2.9\nSS TPM 18.3 19.6 19.0\nMS TPM 19.8 20.1 20.0.\nButt, 34.8 35.5 35.2\nAsh 0.1 0.1 0.1\nSS TPM Wt. 22..4mg 24.4mq 234mg\nMS TPM We. 34.0mg 36. Omg 35. 0mg\n\nOne cigarette has been smoked on the single port smoking machine to\ndetermine mainstream activity data. Mainstream gas phase data is not available\nfor this run. Mainstream TPM weight was 40.6mg. The butt (23mm) was extracted\novernight in 10m) of 1/1 acetone/abs EtOH to yield an activity of 0.88:Ci. The\nTPH pad was sectioned in half: one half was extracted in the acetone/EtOH\nture (found 0.24.Ci = 0.48uCi total MS TPM activity vs 0.42uCi from the total\nrecovery data); the other nalf was subjectea to GC semi-volatile analysis.\nThe usual Uechnique was totally unsuccessful in determining areas or peaks of\nradioactivity. The mass readout was similar to the expected but the radio-\nactivity readout consisted of a continual build-up with no resolved peaks.\nExtraction of the pad after GC analysis yielded 0.085:Ci (35% of the original\n0.24uCi). Additional cigarettes will be analyzed utilizing different parameters.\nAGC-HS Study utilizing non-radioactive a-duvatrienediol is currently underway.\n\nSETSOvOOOT\n\n2. Separation of smoke samples from the Marlboro-Borgwaldt run continues.\nComparisons of eluates from silica and alumina columns were made - in general\nthe alumina column retains more of the smoke constituents. Hexane eluates were\nfound to contain only hydrocarbons with: \"no\" nitrogen containing components.\n\nRK Rre Re Re rrr ee ee eS ee eK eS ee", "words": [{"text": "CHARGE", "x0": 98, "y0": 101, "x1": 142, "y1": 112, "conf": 90.0}, {"text": "NUMBER:", "x0": 151, "y0": 101, "x1": 201, "y1": 111, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "2501", "x0": 266, "y0": 100, "x1": 293, "y1": 111, "conf": 94.0}, {"text": "PROJECT", "x0": 99, "y0": 131, "x1": 150, "y1": 142, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "TITLE:", "x0": 159, "y0": 131, "x1": 201, "y1": 142, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Nuclear", "x0": 266, "y0": 131, "x1": 318, "y1": 142, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "and", "x0": 327, "y0": 131, "x1": 348, "y1": 142, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "Radiochemistry", "x0": 357, "y0": 131, "x1": 462, "y1": 145, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "of", "x0": 471, "y0": 131, "x1": 485, "y1": 142, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Smoke", "x0": 494, "y0": 131, "x1": 530, "y1": 142, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "PROJECT", "x0": 99, "y0": 163, "x1": 150, "y1": 174, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "LEADER:", "x0": 159, "y0": 162, "x1": 209, "y1": 174, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "Roger", "x0": 266, "y0": 163, "x1": 303, "y1": 176, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "A.", "x0": 311, "y0": 162, "x1": 323, "y1": 173, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "Comes", "x0": 334, "y0": 163, "x1": 370, "y1": 174, "conf": 92.0}, {"text": "PERIOD", "x0": 98, "y0": 193, "x1": 143, "y1": 204, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "COVERED:", "x0": 151, "y0": 193, "x1": 209, "y1": 204, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "May", "x0": 265, "y0": 193, "x1": 287, "y1": 206, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "1-31,", "x0": 297, "y0": 192, "x1": 332, "y1": 206, "conf": 95.0}, {"text": "1982", "x0": 343, "y0": 193, "x1": 371, "y1": 204, "conf": 93.0}, {"text": "DATE", "x0": 99, "y0": 224, "x1": 127, "y1": 236, "conf": 96.0}, {"text": "OF", "x0": 136, "y0":